# Docker build context for docker/Dockerfile (context = repository root).
# Deny everything first, then allow only what the image build reads. This keeps the context tiny and keeps
# secrets (.env), databases (*.db*), caches, `.git`, `docs`, fixtures output and other worktrees out of the
# image and out of the layer cache keys.
*

# Rust workspace: manifests, lockfile, cargo config and every crate (including migrations/ for sqlx::migrate!).
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!.cargo
!crates

# Web app (built in the `web` stage).
!web

# Files the runtime image copies in.
!LICENSE
!docker/entrypoint.sh
!docker/healthcheck.sh

# Never ship build output, dependencies or local test artifacts, even inside the allowed trees above.
**/target
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.DS_Store
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/.env
**/.env.*
